from pathlib import Path
import json
base=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
root=base/'client/src/dev/results/torus-lod-alignment-2026-10-28'
s=json.loads((root/'summary.json').read_text());asset='../src/dev/results/torus-lod-alignment-2026-10-28/'
labels={'nature':'Nature','copper-metropolis':'Copper Metropolis','aether-archipelago':'Aether Archipelago'}
common=[];changes=[];cpu_rows=[];images=[];links=[]
for w in s['worlds']:
 terrain=w['terrain'];label=labels[terrain]
 for mode in ['torus','across']:
  n=w['native'][mode];m=w['space']['fixed'][mode];r=m['reference'];t=m['tight']
  common.append(f"<tr><td>{label} / {mode}</td><td>{n['fps']:.1f}</td><td>{n['frame']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{r['fps']:.1f}</td><td>{r['cpu']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{r['gpu']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{t['gpu']['mean']:.3f}</td></tr>")
 for mode,m in w['space']['maintenance'].items():
  r=m['reference'];t=m['cpu']
  cpu_rows.append(f"<tr><td>{label} / {mode}</td><td>{r['terrainCpu']['mean']:.4f} → {t['terrainCpu']['mean']:.4f}</td><td>{m['terrainCpuChangePercent']:+.1f}%</td><td>{r['cpu']['mean']:.3f} → {t['cpu']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{m['cpuChangePercent']:+.1f}%</td></tr>")
 for profile,modes in w['space'].items():
  for mode,m in modes.items():
   r=m['reference'];t=m['cpu'] if profile=='maintenance' else m['tight'];diff=m.get('imageDifference')
   changes.append(f"<tr><td>{label}</td><td>{profile} / {mode}</td><td>{r['gpu']['mean']:.3f} → {t['gpu']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{m['gpuChangePercent']:+.1f}%</td><td>{r['cpu']['mean']:.3f} → {t['cpu']['mean']:.3f}</td><td>{r['faces']:,.0f} → {t['faces']:,.0f}</td><td>{diff['changedPixels'] if diff else 'moving view'}</td></tr>")
 parts=[]
 for mode,index in [('torus',3),('across',2)]:
  pics=[('Native, common 1 m detail',f'minecraft/{terrain}/torus-{index}-{mode}.png'),('Space, common 1 m detail',f'space/fixed/{terrain}/reference-{mode}.png'),('Space, production adaptive LOD',f'space/adaptive/{terrain}/reference-{mode}.png')]
  parts.append('<h3>'+mode+'</h3><div class="pictures">'+''.join(f'<figure><a href="{asset}{path}"><img src="{asset}{path}" alt="{label}, {mode}, {caption}" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>'for caption,path in pics)+'</div>')
 images.append(f'<section class="terrain" data-terrain="{terrain}" {"" if terrain=="copper-metropolis" else "hidden"}>{"".join(parts)}</section>')
 links.append(f'<li>{label}: <a href="{asset}minecraft/{terrain}/torus-minecraft.json.gz">native samples</a>; <a href="{asset}space/fixed/{terrain}/result.json.gz">Space common-detail samples</a>; <a href="{asset}space/adaptive/{terrain}/result.json.gz">Space production-LOD samples</a>; <a href="{asset}space/maintenance/{terrain}/result.json.gz">CPU scheduling samples</a></li>')
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Matched LOD detail and conservative visibility optimization</title>
<style>body{{margin:0;background:#101722;color:#e7edf5;font:16px/1.65 system-ui}}main{{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:48px 28px}}h1{{font-size:42px;line-height:1.15;max-width:900px}}h2{{margin-top:48px}}p{{max-width:1100px;color:#c1cddd}}.tag{{color:#75d9c7;letter-spacing:2px;font-size:12px}}.note{{background:#1c2b3f;border-left:3px solid #75d9c7;padding:18px}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}}th,td{{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #344154;text-align:right}}td:first-child,th:first-child{{text-align:left}}th{{color:#8edccc}}.scroll{{overflow:auto}}a{{color:#8bc7ff}}.pictures{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}}figure{{margin:0}}img{{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}}figcaption{{font-size:13px;color:#aabbd0}}select{{padding:10px;font:inherit;background:#1c2b3f;color:white;border:1px solid #526881}}.terrain[hidden]{{display:none}}@media(max-width:850px){{.pictures{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}h1{{font-size:32px}}}}</style>
<main><div class="tag">CONTROLLED LOD COMPARISON · 28 OCTOBER 2026</div><h1>Matched terrain detail,<br>measured rendering work.</h1><p><a href="#comparison">Common-detail performance</a> · <a href="#cpu">CPU optimization</a> · <a href="#images">Terrain images</a></p>
<p>Nature, Copper Metropolis and Aether Archipelago use the same original terrain export and torus projection. The common reference retains one-metre source cells on both sides, including the opposite patch. Space's ordinary adaptive LOD is tested separately with the same geometry before and after the candidate optimization.</p>
<p class="note"><strong>What is aligned:</strong> standard-cell source detail, fixture coverage, camera, 1280 × 720 rendered pixels, 70° vertical FOV, 8-chunk near radius and 576-chunk far radius. Fog is disabled. DH uses horizontal detail 0 and PIXEL_ART vertical quality; all 512 target sections must be uploaded. Space must load all eight finest sources and select only the 1 m mip. This deliberately removes adaptive LOD loss from the common reference. It does not make the two adaptive hierarchies equivalent.</p>
<p><strong>Remaining differences:</strong> lighting, color transfer, greedy tessellation, near/far blending, graphics API and application/runtime overhead. The fixture contains eight of 128 zones (6.25% area), and microvoxel ornaments are omitted. Minecraft gameplay physics remain flat. The native benchmark disables flight FOV effects and validates the actual projection matrix at 70°; earlier nominal-70° runs were excluded. Native FPS is uncapped; browser presentation is refresh-limited. A native frame interval and a browser GPU pass span are different metrics and do not establish a renderer speed ranking.</p>
<h2>What changes in production</h2><p class="note"><strong>Enable scheduled CPU maintenance; keep tighter idle culling experimental.</strong> Across all three terrains, scheduling reduces the distant-update subspan by 80.4–80.9% while stationary and 56.7–72.1% while turning, saving roughly 0.032–0.045 ms per frame. Complete CPU callbacks improve by 1.6–4.1%; presentation remains around 120 FPS. This is a modest CPU improvement with unchanged geometry, not a demonstrated GPU or FPS speedup. Production LOD and cache budgets stay unchanged.</p>
<p>The tighter-culling candidate reduces stationary near-view face submission by about 24–26%, and improves the adaptive profile's measured GPU span by 16–19%. However, the common-detail Nature and Aether near views regress by 5.0% and 11.1%. It stays off by default. GPU block variance is substantial even in controls with unchanged geometry; the maintenance experiment also has mixed GPU spans, so no stable GPU benefit is claimed.</p>
<h2 id="comparison">Common one-metre detail: measured performance</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Terrain / view</th><th>Native FPS</th><th>Native frame ms</th><th>Space FPS</th><th>Space CPU ms</th><th>Space GPU ms</th><th>Space tighter GPU ms</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(common)}</tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="cpu">CPU scheduling: isolate the work that changed</h2><p>These columns separate the distant voxel update from the complete application frame callback. A large reduction in this small subspan is not the same percentage increase in FPS. Inspect the absolute milliseconds and the two block means in the raw summary.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Terrain / view</th><th>Distant update ms</th><th>Change</th><th>Whole callback ms</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody>{"".join(cpu_rows)}</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Experiments at unchanged LOD</h2><p>The first candidate remains experimental because its GPU result varies with detail level. The existing renderer keeps a broad visibility guard so camera motion can reuse visibility maps. The candidate waits for six unchanged camera/frustum updates, then tightens that guard. Any movement restores the broad guard immediately and invalidates cached tests. Source data, selected mips, face colors, lighting and the optional lossy torus-backface filter are unchanged.</p>
<p>Each view uses reference / candidate / candidate / reference blocks. Each block warms for 5 s and measures for 10 s. The adaptive profile also includes a repeatable turning trajectory. GPU values are asynchronous WebGPU pass envelopes, not total application frame time. Positive percentages mean slower. Screenshot differences compare the two Space variants at the same detail.</p>
<p>The separate <strong>maintenance</strong> profile keeps the original visibility guard and skips repeated batch traversal while resident arena geometry remains unchanged. It resumes work for publication, fading, ownership changes, projection changes and scheduled buffer cleanup. It adds 30 s of steady warmup before measuring. It changes CPU scheduling, with identical selected geometry and images.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Terrain</th><th>Profile / view</th><th>GPU ms</th><th>GPU change</th><th>CPU ms</th><th>Submitted far faces</th><th>Changed image pixels</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(changes)}</tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="images">Inspect detail and reconstruction</h2><p>The first two columns share the one-metre reference; the third shows Space’s normal adaptive policy at the same camera. Full-size images reveal remaining shading and edge-reconstruction differences. Space still shows more fine stippling on island sides, while the native capture has smoother-looking surfaces; matching source detail does not eliminate this visual difference. Within each Space A/B pair, all static captures are compared pixel for pixel; turning captures are not pixel-compared because capture phases differ.</p><select id="terrain" aria-label="Terrain">{''.join(f'<option value="{k}" {"selected" if k=="copper-metropolis" else ""}>{v}</option>'for k,v in labels.items())}</select>{''.join(images)}
<h2>Evidence and reproduction</h2><p><a href="{asset}summary.json">Summary and block results</a> · <a href="{asset}method.json">Method</a> · <a href="{asset}exclusions.json">Excluded attempts</a> · <a href="../../tools/minecraft-torus/README.md">Source and reproduction</a> · <a href="{asset}provenance.json">Provenance</a> · <a href="{asset}validation.json">Final validation and production decision</a></p><ul>{''.join(links)}</ul>
<p>Native runs and browser runs are sequential. Framebuffer mismatches, startup JVM crashes and runs overlapping automated validation are excluded. Source hashes and the prior full-cell validation are reused only for the unchanged disposable saves. The runner verifies complete PNG chunks before archiving screenshots.</p></main><script>document.querySelector('#terrain').addEventListener('change',e=>document.querySelectorAll('.terrain').forEach(s=>s.hidden=s.dataset.terrain!==e.target.value));</script></html>'''
(base/'client/docs/performance-torus-lod-alignment-2026-10-28.html').write_text(html)
